From 6017d751fc1a7a9bf1eac92e2b40b161e0c48b49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TruthProbe <truthprobe@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:33:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/28] feat(desktop): let a fork brand the desktop app

A fork that ships its own Electron application sets OPENCODE_DESKTOP_APP and
OPENCODE_DESKTOP_APP_ID before building. The window title, the AppUserModelID,
the userData directory, the installer product name and the bundle identity then
all follow those two values, and the packaged app stops subscribing to the
upstream updater. Unset, the build is byte-identical in behaviour to before.

The document title moves out of hard-coded strings into app/src/brand.ts, since
Electron takes the window title from document.title rather than the BrowserWindow
option.
