Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:15:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 17/28] fix(truthprobe): drop phi and the worst token from the
 default score

Measured on 626 rows (544 truthful, 82 deliberate lies): the old
0.4*geo+0.3*worst+0.3*phi formula gave AUROC 0.388, i.e. worse than
chance, because phi anti-correlates with correctness (0.199 alone).
exp(meanLp) alone gives 0.597 and ECE 0.098 on the same rows, and
ECE 0.160 instead of 0.493 on 739 truthful rows.

phi and minLp stay as features for fitted models; they just no longer
drive the built-in score.
