From: vladmurnik <vladmurnik@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:49:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 26/28] fix(truthprobe): close the nine findings from the
 external audit

- digitDensity divides by code points, not UTF-16 units; a flag emoji or an
  astral CJK no longer halves the measured digit share
- minOf replaces Math.min(...values) in both feature and sentence paths: a
  long answer could throw RangeError inside event publication
- offset drift keeps the score visible in one pseudo-sentence instead of an
  empty sentence list that reads as "nothing doubtful"
- features carry the raw mean logprob; log(max(geo, 1e-9)) collapsed every
  poor answer into -20.7 and cost the linear model its resolution
- a doubtful sentence is flagged on strict risk > riskyThreshold, so the flag
  can no longer disagree with the level on the 0.55/0.45 boundary
- session-ui and TUI read LEVEL_BOUNDS from @opencode/core instead of
  repeating the numbers (session-ui gains the workspace dependency)
- a reasoning-token score is reported as "partial", and the TUI says so
- TRUTHPROBE_SHAKY_THRESHOLD is removed: nothing ever read it
