 version

splitStamp('2.0.32+') returned the whole string as the version, so the service
comparison would fail exactly like the bug this split exists to fix. The version
is now always the text before the separator; a leading plus means the file
carries no version at all and is treated as unstamped.

Tests: the trailing-plus case expects the truncated version, keptStages keeps a
stamped stage directory, and an invariant test asserts the compared version
never contains '+'.
